Approach: Use sliding window with two pointers. Expand right, count zeros, and shrink from left when zeros exceed k to maintain valid window, tracking maximum length.

Time Complexity: O(n) — each element is visited at most twice (left and right pointers).

Space Complexity: O(1) — only variables used, no extra space.

class Solution {
    public int longestOnes(int[] arr, int k) {
        int left=0,right=0,n=arr.length,maxlen=0,count=0;
        while(right<n){
           if(arr[right]==0){
            count++;
           }
            if(count>k){
                if(arr[left]==0){
                    count--;
                }
                left++;
            }
           if(count<=k){
            maxlen=Math.max(maxlen,right-left+1);
           }
           right++;
        }
        return maxlen;
